From: Josip Seketa <josip.seketa@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 00:00:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 29/45] gdb/remote: don't throw from the scope exit in
 process_initial_stop_replies

A connection lost during a non-stop connect made the scope exit throw on the exec target: an internal error.

diff --git a/gdb/remote.c b/gdb/remote.c
index fcca5873ea7..4210446f26e 100644
--- a/gdb/remote.c
+++ b/gdb/remote.c
@@ -5229,9 +5229,28 @@ remote_target::process_initial_stop_replies (int from_tty)
 	   the poll in stop_all_threads to consider events from it, so enable
 	   it temporarily.  */
 	gdb_assert (!this->is_async_p ());
-	SCOPE_EXIT { target_async (false); };
 	target_async (true);
+
+	/* If an error leaves stop_all_threads, disable async on the way
+	   out.  This must not throw.  If the connection was lost, the
+	   remote target is gone by then, and this fails too; the error
+	   being thrown already says why.  Otherwise, disable it below,
+	   where an error can be reported.  */
+	auto disable_on_error = make_scope_exit ([] ()
+	  {
+	    try
+	      {
+		target_async (false);
+	      }
+	    catch (const gdb_exception &)
+	      {
+	      }
+	  });
+
 	stop_all_threads ("remote connect in all-stop");
+
+	disable_on_error.release ();
+	target_async (false);
       }
 
       /* If all threads of an inferior were already stopped, we
